{{!
    @template block_nit_offers/bar

    A one-line announcement bar for the offers currently running on the site.

    Every row is rendered; the active one is shown and the rest wait behind it, so
    switching offers is a class change with no re-render and no layout jump. All of
    the horizontal layout uses logical properties, so the bar mirrors itself in
    Arabic without a second stylesheet.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * barid — unique DOM id for this block instance
    * fingerprint — id of the current offer set, remembered by the dismiss button
    * tone — brand colour role tinting the bar (accent | primary | success | warning)
    * flag — the small pill at the start of the bar, e.g. "Offer"
    * rotate — cycle automatically between rows
    * multiple — more than one row (renders the dots)
    * dismissible — render the close button
    * dismisslabel — accessible name for that button
    * showlabel — accessible name pattern for a dot, with {index} already applied
    * rows — the offers: index, first, headline, badge, meta, scope, url, linktext

    Example context (json):
    {
        "barid": "nitoff-1",
        "fingerprint": "a1b2c3d4e5f6",
        "tone": "accent",
        "flag": "Offer",
        "rotate": true,
        "multiple": false,
        "dismissible": true,
        "dismisslabel": "Dismiss this announcement",
        "rows": [
            {
                "index": 1,
                "first": true,
                "headline": "Autumn intake — 25% off Logistics courses",
                "badge": "-25%",
                "meta": "Ends 30 September",
                "scope": "Applies to: All courses",
                "url": "https://example.com/catalogue",
                "linktext": "See courses"
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div id="{{barid}}" class="nitoff nitoff--{{tone}}{{#multiple}} nitoff--multi{{/multiple}}"
     data-nitoff data-fingerprint="{{fingerprint}}"{{#rotate}} data-rotate="1"{{/rotate}}>
    <div class="nitoff__inner">
        <span class="nitoff__flag">{{flag}}</span>

        <div class="nitoff__track">
            {{#rows}}
            <div class="nitoff__item{{#first}} is-active{{/first}}" data-nitoff-item data-index="{{index}}">
                <span class="nitoff__headline">{{{headline}}}</span>
                {{#badge}}<span class="nitoff__badge">{{badge}}</span>{{/badge}}
                {{#meta}}<span class="nitoff__meta">{{meta}}</span>{{/meta}}
                {{#scope}}<span class="nitoff__scope">{{scope}}</span>{{/scope}}
                {{#url}}<a class="nitoff__cta" href="{{url}}">{{linktext}}</a>{{/url}}
            </div>
            {{/rows}}
        </div>

        {{#multiple}}
        <div class="nitoff__dots" role="tablist">
            {{#rows}}
            <button type="button" class="nitoff__dot{{#first}} is-active{{/first}}" data-nitoff-dot
                    data-index="{{index}}" role="tab" aria-selected="{{#first}}true{{/first}}{{^first}}false{{/first}}"
                    aria-label="{{showlabel}} {{index}}"></button>
            {{/rows}}
        </div>
        {{/multiple}}

        {{#dismissible}}
        <button type="button" class="nitoff__close" data-nitoff-close aria-label="{{dismisslabel}}">
            <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
        </button>
        {{/dismissible}}
    </div>
</div>
